# Central copy

The working copy for account `julian-holtom` is https://cursor.com/codebase/julian-holtom. Treat that list as the place another signed-in machine should open.

At the start of work on an existing project, fetch the central copy and continue from it when it is newer than the files on this computer.

After changing project files, before ending the task:

1. Leave out secrets: `.env`, credentials, tokens, and private keys.
2. If a remote already points at `origin.cursor.com/julian-holtom/<name>`, commit and push the current branch there.
3. If the project still uses GitHub, keep that remote. Push the same commit to the `cursor` remote. Do not replace the GitHub remote.
4. If no central copy exists, create a private repository under `julian-holtom` named after the folder, then push the working branch.
5. Do not force-push. Do not change git config. Sign in with the existing Cursor account. Do not install another system to do this.

Example: this theme pushes to `https://origin.cursor.com/julian-holtom/directmx-shopify.git`. A GitHub project such as PAYE-1 keeps GitHub and also pushes to `https://origin.cursor.com/julian-holtom/paye-1.git`.
